 "stem": "If $\\overleftrightarrow{AB}\\parallel\\overleftrightarrow{CD}$ where $A({=x1}, {=y1})$, $B({=x2}, {=y2})$, $C({=x3}, {=y3})$ and $D({=x4}, k)$, find the value of $k$.",
 "answer": "k",
 "solution": [
  "Slope of $\\overleftrightarrow{AB}$ = $\\frac{{=y2} - ({=y1})}{{=x2} - ({=x1})} = {=m}$.",
  "Slope of $\\overleftrightarrow{CD}$ = $\\frac{k - ({=y3})}{{=x4} - ({=x3})} = \\frac{k - ({=y3})}{{=e}}$.",
  "The lines are parallel, so their slopes are equal: $\\frac{k - ({=y3})}{{=e}} = {=m}$.",
  "Then $k - ({=y3}) = {=m * e}$, so $k = {=k}$."
 ],
